  "commentary": "Sweden's founding membership in the Ukraine Aggression Tribunal lands on a recovering but fragile fiscal base: GDP growth returned to 0.82% in 2024 after the 2023 contraction (-0.20%), following the post-invasion pattern of 1.26% in 2022 and the 5.23% rebound year of 2021. With nominal GDP near USD 604 billion, the SEK 30–80 million annual tribunal contribution amounts to well under 0.01% of national output — a scale argument the government can deploy against cost-framing disinformation. Inflation, which surged to 8.37% (2022) and 8.55% (2023) during the Ukraine-war energy shock, normalised to 2.84% in 2024, easing the cost-of-living pressures Russian influence operations exploit with \"Ukraine costs Sweden money\" narratives. Sweden's USD 57,117 GDP per capita in 2024 places it between Finland (USD 55,872) and Denmark (USD 69,290) — well inside the Nordic high-income band that underwrites an equitable burden-sharing formula for founding-member tribunal dues alongside Norway's USD 88,660.",
